<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Shakar Kheda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1724">1724</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Shakar Kheda was fought on 11 October 1724 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berar">Berar</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-jah-i">Nizam-ul-Mulk</a>, the future Asaf Jah I, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mubariz-khan">Mubariz Khan</a>, the Mughal governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> backed by the court. Nizam-ul-Mulk won, and Mubariz Khan was killed. The victory made the Nizam master of the Deccan and marked the founding of Hyderabad State.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shakar-kheda.jpg" alt="Battle of Shakar Kheda" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jadunath Sarkar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Shakar_Khera.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
